.TH tkupdfinspect n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkupdfinspect
.PP
Read\-only PDF structure inspector widget: a two\-pane frame with a structure tree on the left and a read\-only detail pane on the right. The structure is read through \fBtclutils::tupdf\fR; the widget never modifies the file. Pure Tk/ttk; namespace \fB::tkutils::tkupdfinspect\fR.
.SS API
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::widget .w ?-width N? ?-height N?]  ;# -> frame path
::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::loadFile    $w path   ;# inspect file, fill tree -> path
::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::currentFile $w        ;# last loaded file ("" if none)
::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::summary     $w        ;# cached summary dict from last load
::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::treeWidget  $w        ;# path of the structure tree
::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::textWidget  $w        ;# path of the read-only detail text
.CE
.SS "Widget options"
.PP
\fBwidget\fR returns the frame \fB$path\fR it creates (a \fBttk::frame\fR holding a horizontal \fBttk::panedwindow\fR: structure tree on the left, detail text on the right). \fB\-width\fR and \fB\-height\fR (default \fB64\fR x \fB24\fR) size the detail text widget in characters and lines.
.SS "Structure tree"
.PP
\fBloadFile\fR reads the file via \fBtclutils::tupdf\fR and populates the tree with the top\-level nodes \fBDocument\fR, \fBMetadata\fR, \fBTrailer\fR, \fBZUGFeRD\fR, and \fBObjects (N)\fR, the last expanding to one \fBobj <id>\fR child per object. Selecting a node renders its detail into the right\-hand pane. After a load the \fBDocument\fR node is selected automatically, so the summary is shown immediately. \fBcurrentFile\fR returns the loaded path and \fBsummary\fR returns the summary dict that was cached during the load, without re\-reading the file.
.SS "Read\-only and errors"
.PP
The detail pane is not editable and nothing is ever written back to the file. For non\-PDF input, \fBtclutils::tupdf\fR raises \fB{TCLUTILS TUPDF FORMAT}\fR; \fBloadFile\fR lets that error surface so the caller can report it.
.CS
package require tkutils::tkupdfinspect
set w [::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::widget .ins]
pack $w -fill both -expand 1
if {[catch {::tkutils::tkupdfinspect::loadFile $w invoice.pdf} err opts]} {
    if {[lrange [dict get $opts -errorcode] 0 1] eq {TCLUTILS TUPDF}} {
        tk_messageBox -message "Not a readable PDF: $err"
    }
}
.CE
